1
00:00:00,030 --> 00:00:02,030
One small box just stopped every plane in

2
00:00:02,030 --> 00:00:03,840
America from taking off.

3
00:00:03,870 --> 00:00:07,050
November 13th, only the third time ever.

4
00:00:07,270 --> 00:00:09,500
The first was 9/11.

5
00:00:09,550 --> 00:00:11,950
So how does one box do that?

6
00:00:12,030 --> 00:00:14,600
Planes already in the air kept flying.

7
00:00:14,630 --> 00:00:17,030
But for over four hours, nothing new took

8
00:00:17,090 --> 00:00:17,520
off.

9
00:00:17,550 --> 00:00:18,640
Here's why.

10
00:00:18,670 --> 00:00:20,800
In the air, you're guided by one of 22

11
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:22,720
hidden control centers.

12
00:00:22,750 --> 00:00:25,140
Controllers there keep planes apart by

13
00:00:25,140 --> 00:00:25,840
talking.

14
00:00:25,950 --> 00:00:28,690
That afternoon, 17 of the 22 started

15
00:00:28,690 --> 00:00:30,120
losing those lines.

16
00:00:30,150 --> 00:00:32,180
A controller who can't talk can't keep

17
00:00:32,180 --> 00:00:35,120
planes apart, so departures stopped.

18
00:00:35,150 --> 00:00:36,710
Was it a cyber attack?

19
00:00:36,790 --> 00:00:38,720
Officials say no.

20
00:00:38,750 --> 00:00:40,990
At one site, contractor L3 Harris was

21
00:00:41,030 --> 00:00:43,130
switching copper lines to fiber.

22
00:00:43,230 --> 00:00:45,470
One router began flooding the network.

23
00:00:45,510 --> 00:00:48,610
Over 1,000 requests every five seconds.

24
00:00:48,750 --> 00:00:50,580
Investigators still don't know if it was

25
00:00:50,580 --> 00:00:52,800
faulty or installed wrong.

26
00:00:52,830 --> 00:00:55,930
One box, a whole country grounded.

27
00:00:56,110 --> 00:00:57,280
Follow for mores.
